  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES. All four shapes reproduce; two of the item's stated causes are imprecise.\nREPRO (hidar fixtures copied to a scratch dir, fresh XDG cache each, hypergumbo verify-claims --claims claims_pt.yaml --json + survey):\n- j_local control: doFinal dst java:javax.crypto.Cipher:0-0:doFinal, violated, evidence_count 1.\n- j_chain (shape 1): dst java:external:0-0:doFinal, inconclusive [unknown_receiver_scope].\n- j_var (shape 2): dst java:external:0-0:doFinal, inconclusive [unknown_receiver_scope].\n- j_fq (shape 3): dst java:external:0-0:doFinal, confirmed_with_caveats [unknown_receiver_scope].\n- new fixture, Cipher param + new FileOutputStream(\"out.bin\").write(pt) (shape 4): write dst java:external:0-0:write, inconclusive [untyped_receiver, unknown_receiver_scope].\nWI-dorus (a9da22c29a) does NOT bear on this: it types only the System.out/System.err field-access receiver (_java_std_output_receiver, java.py ~887).\nCAUSE CORRECTIONS:\n- Shapes 1/2: the item says the registry holds only project methods. Since WI-lalot (3e04093160, 09-04) method_return_type_registry also merges library_signatures/java.yaml rows (java.py ~3824). That catalogue has no Cipher.getInstance row, AND a row alone is not enough: a fixture using an EXISTING row (Files.newOutputStream -> java.io.OutputStream) still emits java:external:0-0:write for both Files.newOutputStream(p).write(b) and var o = Files.newOutputStream(p); o.write(b). Reason: _chained_receiver_type (java.py 2323) takes an owner only from var_types or a PROJECT class (class_symbols), never from an imported external class; and _declared_type_name (816) returns None for var with no initializer inference arm for a static external call. Fix needs both: rows + the lookup arm.\n- Shape 3: the precise cause is _extract_param_types (java.py 505; type match at 536) accepting type_identifier/generic_type/array_type but not scoped_type_identifier. A fully-qualified LOCAL (javax.crypto.Cipher c = ...) already types correctly via _declared_type_name (checked: dst java:javax.crypto.Cipher:0-0:doFinal). Parameters do not go through _declared_type_name.\n- Shape 4: no object_creation_expression receiver arm in the call emitter; confirmed by repro, cause not otherwise re-examined.\nCorpus frequency of each shape: not measured (as in the filing).\nRelated: WI-jubim (kotlin/scala do not consume library signatures), WI-buvob (java crypto rows), WI-monul (receiver_type_hint unread)."  # efc2
- op: update  # 5394
  at: '2026-10-01T01:32:03Z'  # 5394
  by: agent  # 5394
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5394
  clock: 3  # 5394
  nonce: '5394'  # 5394
  set:  # 5394
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-25 re-measuring WI-hidar on the production path. Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/hidar_09252026/RESULT.md (fixtures j_*, one repo + XDG cache each).\n\nThe java analyzer types a method-call receiver from a declared parameter, a declared local (INV-vugon), a field, this.field and a wildcard import: in each, c.doFinal(ct) emits dst java:javax.crypto.Cipher:0-0:doFinal and the plaintext -> host_fs claim is violated with 1 finding. FOUR ORDINARY SHAPES emit dst java:external instead, so no catalogued method row can match them:\n\n  1. chained static-factory return      Cipher.getInstance(\"AES\").doFinal(ct)       -> external; verdict inconclusive, 0 findings\n  2. var bound from a static factory     var c = Cipher.getInstance(\"AES\"); c.doFinal(ct)  -> external; inconclusive, 0 findings\n  3. fully-qualified parameter type, no import   void dec(javax.crypto.Cipher c, ..) { c.doFinal(ct) }  -> external; confirmed_with_caveats [unknown_receiver_scope], 0 findings\n  4. constructor-expression receiver     new FileOutputStream(\"out.bin\").write(pt)  -> the write is untyped (untyped_receiver caveat), so the SINK does not match; the declared-local spelling of the same sink does\n\nControl: the same file without the doFinal call is confirmed, 0 findings.\n\nCAUSES (java.py, relocate by name):\n- Shapes 1 and 2. method_return_type_registry already merges library rows from library_signatures/java.yaml (WI-lalot, merged after the analysed rows). That catalogue has no Cipher.getInstance row, but adding one is NECESSARY, NOT SUFFICIENT: with an existing row (Files.newOutputStream -> java.io.OutputStream), both Files.newOutputStream(p).write(b) and var o = Files.newOutputStream(p); o.write(b) still emit java:external:0-0:write. Shape 1: _chained_receiver_type takes the inner call's owner only from var_types or a PROJECT class (class_symbols), never from an imported external class, so the registry is not consulted. Shape 2: _declared_type_name returns None for var, and no arm infers a var local's type from a static external call through the registry.\n- Shape 3. _extract_param_types matches type_identifier / generic_type / array_type but not scoped_type_identifier, so a qualified PARAMETER type binds nothing. A qualified LOCAL (javax.crypto.Cipher c = ...) already types, because locals go through _declared_type_name.\n- Shape 4. The call emitter has no object_creation_expression receiver arm (INV-misup did this for javascript).\n\nSCOPE: measured on one source row (Cipher.doFinal) and one sink row (FileOutputStream.write). Each shape is a receiver-typing gap, so it applies to every method-kind java catalogue row reached that way; the corpus frequency of each shape has NOT been counted. WI-dorus (System.out / System.err typed as PrintStream) does not touch these shapes.\n\nDIRECTION: none of the four produces a bare confirmed in these fixtures (inconclusive x2, confirmed_with_caveats x1, untyped_receiver caveat x1). It is a recall gap that the verdicts disclose, not a false all-clear.\n\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # 5394
- op: discuss  # d41e
